  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a parabola <math><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> with vertex at <math><mi>A</mi></math> and focus at <math><mi>S</mi><mo>.</mo></math> <math><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is a chord of the parabola which is normal at point <math><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo></math> If the abscissa and the ordinate of the point <math><mi>P</mi></math> are equal, then the square of the length of the diameter of the circumcircle of triangle <math><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "125",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/8ad2ad65-d459-428c-82c9-3e80ede44fac.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width:3.12014in;height:1.80694in\" /></p><p><math><msubsup><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br />So, <math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;and <math><mi>Q</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Slope of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>6</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>S</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>Q</mi><mi>S</mi></math><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math> is the diameter of the circle passing through <math><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi></mi><mi>Q</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />Hence, the length of the diameter <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>100</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>125</mn></msqrt></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;square of the length of the diameter<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>125</mn></math></p>",
    "image": null
